---
pagination:
  data: loanAmounts
  size: 1
  alias: loan
permalink: "/emi-for-{{ loan.slug }}-home-loan/"
layout: layouts/base.njk
usesChart: true
updated: 2026-09-10
eleventyComputed:
  title: "EMI for {{ loan.label }} Home Loan — Monthly Payment & Interest"
  description: "EMI for a {{ loan.label }} home loan at every rate and tenure, with total interest, salary needed and a live amortization schedule."
---
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
{% set tenures = [10, 15, 20, 25, 30] %}
{% set rates = [8, 8.5, 9, 9.5] %}
{% set heroEmi = loan.amount | emiFor(loan.headlineRate, loan.headlineYears) %}
{% set heroInterest = loan.amount | emiTotalInterest(loan.headlineRate, loan.headlineYears) %}

<div class="wrap page-pad">
  <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">›</span> <a href="/emi-calculator/">EMI Calculator</a> <span aria-hidden="true">›</span> <span>{{ loan.label }} home loan</span></nav>
  <h1>EMI for a {{ loan.label }} home loan</h1>
  <p class="lede">A {{ loan.label }} home loan at {{ loan.headlineRate }}% for {{ loan.headlineYears }} years costs about <strong>{{ heroEmi | inr }} a month</strong>, with roughly <strong>{{ heroInterest | compactInr }}</strong> paid in interest over the full tenure. Change the rate and tenure below to match your own offer.</p>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: {{ updated | readableDate }}</p>

  <div class="calc">
    <div class="inputs">
      {{ m.field('p', 'Loan amount', '₹', 100000, 100000000, 100000, loan.amount, '₹1L', '₹10 Cr') }}
      {{ m.field('r', 'Interest rate (p.a.)', '%', 5, 15, 0.05, loan.headlineRate, '5%', '15%') }}
      {{ m.field('n', 'Tenure', 'years', 1, 30, 1, loan.headlineYears, '1 yr', '30 yrs') }}
      <div class="result-actions"><button class="btn-ghost" data-copylink>Copy link to this calculation</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="results">
      <div class="stat-row">
        <div class="stat hero"><div class="k">Monthly EMI</div><div class="v" id="out-emi">—</div><div class="sub" id="out-emi-sub"></div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">Total interest</div><div class="v" id="out-int">—</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">Total repayment</div><div class="v" id="out-total">—</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">Income needed</div><div class="v" id="out-income">—</div><div class="sub">EMI ≈ 40% of take-home</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-box" style="height:180px"><canvas id="chart-split"></canvas></div>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart-bal"></canvas></div>
      <p class="chart-note">Outstanding balance at the end of each year.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <details class="sched">
    <summary>Amortization schedule (year by year)</summary>
    <div id="sched-out"></div>
  </details>

  <article class="article">
    <h2>What a {{ loan.label }} home loan really costs</h2>
    <p>{{ loan.context }}</p>
    <p>The table below shows the monthly EMI for a {{ loan.label }} loan at the rates lenders are realistically quoting, across every common tenure. Find your offered rate along the top and your tenure down the side.</p>

    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Tenure</th>
            {% for r in rates %}<th>{{ r }}%</th>{% endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for t in tenures %}
          <tr>
            <th>{{ t }} years</th>
            {% for r in rates %}<td>{{ loan.amount | emiForInr(r, t) }}</td>{% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="chart-note">Monthly EMI on a {{ loan.label }} loan, reducing-balance method.</p>

    <h2>Total interest by tenure</h2>
    <p>The EMI is only half the story. Stretching the tenure lowers the monthly figure but raises what the loan costs in total — often dramatically:</p>

    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Tenure at {{ loan.headlineRate }}%</th><th>Monthly EMI</th><th>Total interest</th><th>Total repaid</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for t in tenures %}
          <tr>
            <th>{{ t }} years</th>
            <td>{{ loan.amount | emiForInr(loan.headlineRate, t) }}</td>
            <td>{{ loan.amount | emiTotalInterest(loan.headlineRate, t) | compactInr }}</td>
            <td>{{ (loan.amount + (loan.amount | emiTotalInterest(loan.headlineRate, t))) | compactInr }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>What salary do you need?</h2>
    <p>Lenders generally want your total EMIs to stay within 40–50% of net monthly income. For a {{ loan.label }} loan at {{ loan.headlineRate }}% over {{ loan.headlineYears }} years, that points to a take-home income of roughly <strong>{{ loan.incomeNeeded }} a month</strong>, assuming you carry no other significant EMIs. A co-applicant's income can be combined to improve eligibility, which is why joint applications are common.</p>

    <h2>How the EMI is calculated</h2>
    <div class="formula">EMI = P × r × (1 + r)<sup>n</sup> / ((1 + r)<sup>n</sup> − 1)</div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>P</strong> — {{ loan.label }}, the loan amount</li>
      <li><strong>r</strong> — monthly rate = annual rate ÷ 12 ÷ 100</li>
      <li><strong>n</strong> — tenure in months</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This is the reducing-balance method every Indian bank and housing finance company uses: interest each month is charged only on the outstanding principal, which falls with every payment.</p>

    <h2>Reducing what you pay</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Prepay in the early years.</strong> The interest share of each EMI is highest at the start, so early prepayments buy far more than late ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep the EMI, cut the tenure.</strong> When you prepay, choosing to shorten the tenure rather than reduce the EMI saves substantially more interest.</li>
      <li><strong>Negotiate or transfer.</strong> Floating-rate home loans for individuals carry no prepayment or foreclosure penalty under RBI rules, so a balance transfer to a cheaper lender is always on the table.</li>
      <li><strong>Compare on the reducing-balance rate</strong>, never a flat rate — a 10% flat rate is roughly equivalent to 18–19% reducing balance.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <section class="faq-section" id="faqs">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    {% for f in loan.faqs %}
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>{{ f.q }}</summary>
      <p>{{ f.a }}</p>
    </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  <section class="related-section">
    <h2>Other loan amounts</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {% for l in loanAmounts %}{% if l.slug != loan.slug %}
      <a class="calc-card" href="/emi-for-{{ l.slug }}-home-loan/">
        <span class="calc-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">🏠</span>
        <span class="calc-card-name">{{ l.label }} home loan EMI</span>
        <span class="calc-card-short">Monthly EMI, total interest and salary needed for a {{ l.label }} loan.</span>
      </a>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>

    <h2>Related calculators</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {% for slug in ["emi-calculator", "income-tax-calculator", "sip-calculator"] %}
        {% set rc = calcs | calcBySlug(slug) %}
        {% if rc %}
        <a class="calc-card" href="/{{ rc.slug }}/">
          <span class="calc-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ rc.icon }}</span>
          <span class="calc-card-name">{{ rc.name }}</span>
          <span class="calc-card-short">{{ rc.short }}</span>
        </a>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "{{ site.url }}/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "EMI Calculator", "item": "{{ site.url }}/emi-calculator/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "{{ loan.label }} home loan EMI", "item": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}" }
  ]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {% for f in loan.faqs %}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ f.q | dump | safe }},
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ f.a | dump | safe }} }
    }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

<script>
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
  function recalc() {
    var p = CM.val('p'), rate = CM.val('r'), yrs = CM.val('n');
    var r = rate / 1200, n = Math.round(yrs * 12);
    if (p <= 0 || n <= 0) return;

    var emi = r === 0 ? p / n : p * r * Math.pow(1 + r, n) / (Math.pow(1 + r, n) - 1);
    var total = emi * n, totInt = total - p;

    CM.set('out-emi', CM.inr(emi));
    CM.set('out-emi-sub', 'for ' + CM.num(yrs, 0) + ' years at ' + CM.num(rate, 2) + '%');
    CM.set('out-int', CM.inr(totInt));
    CM.set('out-total', CM.inr(total));
    CM.set('out-income', CM.inr(emi / 0.4));

    CM.doughnut('chart-split', ['Principal', 'Interest'], [p, totInt], ['--s1', '--s3']);

    var bal = p, labels = ['Y0'], balSeries = [p], rows = [];
    var yInt = 0, yPr = 0, year = 1;
    for (var mth = 1; mth <= n; mth++) {
      var i = bal * r, pr = emi - i;
      bal = Math.max(0, bal - pr);
      yInt += i; yPr += pr;
      if (mth % 12 === 0 || mth === n) {
        labels.push('Y' + year); balSeries.push(bal);
        rows.push([year, CM.inr(yPr), CM.inr(yInt), CM.inr(bal)]);
        yInt = 0; yPr = 0; year++;
      }
    }
    CM.lineChart('chart-bal', labels, [{ label: 'Outstanding balance', data: balSeries, role: '--s1', fill: true }]);
    CM.table('sched-out', ['Year', 'Principal paid', 'Interest paid', 'Balance'], rows);
  }
  CM.bind(['p', 'r', 'n'], recalc);
});
</script>
